    "title": "真 / 有: 真有你/他/她的 evaluates a surprising performance; tone determines praise or criticism",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk5-stance-frames-p02-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "真 / 有: 真有你/他/她的 evaluates a surprising performance; tone determines praise or criticism",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "This fixed reaction evaluates a surprising performance. Context and tone can make it praise or sarcasm; the final particle does not mark possession. 真有你的 may also be sarcastic criticism after an inconsiderate act; relationship and preceding context determine it. Do not use it as a reliably polite compliment.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "你答对了，真有你的！",
                "pinyin": "nǐ dá duì le ， zhēn yǒu nǐ de ！",
                "meaning": "You got the answer right—impressive!",
                "audio": "8b8f2d191247215b71ed379f3be9cac61f6ffda4e8c2139358cfbae2ffd8832b"
              },
              {
                "text": "你又忘了我的名字，真有你的！",
                "pinyin": "nǐ yòu wàng le wǒ de míngzi ， zhēn yǒu nǐ de ！",
                "meaning": "You have forgotten my name again. Well, that is just great of you! Sarcastic criticism, not praise.",
                "audio": "75a07ada6c73a4e5c6c1f8283adf47e5d791393371defc5316342a250699b464"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
